# Windows Weld E2 receipt. The viewer is pinned before content comes alive, so
# the captured frame can only be the CEF producer rather than Turnstone's
# existing genet.web session lane. Run with --features weld, TURNSTONE_CEF_PATH,
# and a fresh TURNSTONE_ROOT.
settle 30
key escape

open https://example.com/
settle 40
assert visible
assert focused example.com

act Open Apparatus pane
settle 5
assert pane apparatus
click-row weld.chromium
settle 5
assert event viewer-changed

act Toggle live content
settle 90
assert content-live
assert surface content
capture 01_weld_example

# Click example.com's visible "Learn more" link inside the CEF tile. This is
# the same content-pointer seam winit drives; the resulting page transition is
# visible evidence that Chromium received the input. The focused assertion and
# semantic event prove the CEF commit also changed this same graph member.
move-at 310 303
settle 10
assert event surface-cursor
click-at 310 303
settle 40
assert content-live
assert surface content
assert focused iana.org/help/example-domains
assert event content-navigated
capture 02_weld_after_input
log E2 Weld Windows frame, input, and navigation receipt complete
